  "body": "Process change: the P0/P1/P2 scale becomes P1-P9 (lower number is picked first). **PROCESS_VERSION 29** (another process PR takes 28 and merges first; the merger renumbers if needed).\r\n\r\n## Scale (AGENTS.md \"Priorities\")\r\n| Label | Means | Was |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `P1` | Unsafe or wrong output, crash, data loss | `P0` |\r\n| `P2` | Main broken / regression with no workaround | red-gate `P1` |\r\n| `P3` | Wrong behaviour a user hits, with a workaround | `P1` bugs |\r\n| `P4` | Work the maintainer asked for | `P1` enhancements he opened |\r\n| `P5` | Agent surface and tooling (MCP, process) | `P1` MCP / process |\r\n| `P6` | Accepted enhancements, not scheduled | other `P1` enhancements |\r\n| `P7` | Owed polish, small fixes | `P2` bugs and polish |\r\n| `P8` | Ideas needing design/research | `P2` enhancements, `effort:max` |\r\n| `P9` | Someday | - |\r\n\r\nOnly `P1` and `P2` block a release cut (maintainer's later choice); `P3` is worked ahead of planned work but never holds a cut.\r\n\r\n## Rules changed (old -> new)\r\n- Pick: \"`P0` before `P1` before `P2`, then the oldest\" -> lowest number first, then the oldest.\r\n- `P?`: \"instead of a `P0`/`P1`/`P2` label\" / \"picks `P0`/`P1`/`P2`\" -> `P1`..`P9`.\r\n- Enhancement lane: \"then `P1` before `P2`\" -> \"then the lower number\".\r\n- Safety floor: \"every `P0`\" -> \"every `P1`\" is at least `effort:high`.\r\n- MCP issues: `P1` -> `P5` (the 2026-11-10 quote kept, dated).\r\n- Red batch gate: \"`P0` if wrong output or gouge, else `P1`\" -> `P1` / `P2`; cut blocker \"a `P0` it opened\" -> any open `P1` or `P2` (wide reading, per the maintainer; a `P3` never) - superseded the first draft, which kept \"it opened\".\r\n- New filing rules: `P1`-`P3` defects only; `P4` only with the maintainer's words quoted; follow-ups are `P7` unless a defect; never `P?`.\r\n\r\n## Files\r\n`AGENTS.md`, `README.md`, `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION`, `.claude/skills/{gh-issues (SKILL, claim-workflow, both evals), classify-effort, camcraft-mcp}`, `docs/decisions/1189-p1-p9-scale.md` (decision + migration script). work-issue, review-prs, resolve-conflicts, agents, issue templates, CONTRIBUTING (absent), docs/ and `xtask/src` name no priority level (xtask reads no priority labels; no xtask test run needed). The pick-next jq `test(\"^P[0-9]$\")` already matches P1..P9; its default for unlabelled became `PZ` so it does not tie with `P9`.\r\n\r\n## Grep\r\n`grep -rn \"P0\" AGENTS.md .claude .github README.md`: only AGENTS.md:93 and :100 (the quoted maintainer words and the \"Was\" column) and two Stripe URLs containing `P0F...`. Evals parse as YAML.\r\n\r\n## No label or issue was changed by this PR\r\nThe migration script is in the decision file; the merging session runs it once (`--dry-run` first) right after the merge, then comments on #681 with the mapping. The \"main is broken\" `P2` set is an explicit `--main-broken` list, not guessed from labels.\r\n\r\n**Fork:** pull the process files, create the same labels, relabel its own issues with the same mapping (old `P1` first, then `P0` -> `P1`).\r\n\r\nChangelog: none\r\nEffort: medium\r\n\r\nFixes #1189\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n## Rework after review (head after this push)\r\n1. Cut rule: one sentence, same words in \"Priorities\" and \"Fixes are tested in the background\": a minor/major cut does not start while any `P1` or `P2` issue is open (a `P3` or lower never holds one). Decision file corrected.\r\n2. MCP: `P5` is owed agent-surface work; a defect in MCP code is rated `P1`-`P3`.\r\n3. No priority = untriaged: triaged by the first agent that reads it, before any pick; both gh-issues Pick snippets list such issues first under \"TRIAGE THESE FIRST\" and exclude `P?`; an issue found with two numbers is reported and read by the lower.\r\n4. claim-workflow.md agrees with SKILL.md (\"lowest P number first\"; no `P9` default); pick-next eval updated.\r\n5-8. Migration script rewritten: `P?` issues never get a number (stray `P2` beside `P?` removed and listed); `--main-broken` and `--requested` are explicit lists, with area:build bug candidates printed; old `P1` order bug (`P3`/`P2`), requested (`P4`), mcp/build/process (`P5`), else `P6`; old `P2` enhancements `P8` (`P6` only with an open PR linked); idempotent via a plan file with a per-row done flag, refusing with \"migration already started: pass the plan file (--plan FILE)\"; `P0` kept and re-described as retired, never deleted; end-state assertions and counts. Its `--dry-run` was run read-only against the repo to test it.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n## Re-check follow-ups (head 78681207)\r\n- Merged main; PROCESS_VERSION stays 29 (main reads 28).\r\n- Old-`P1` issues without `bug` that are `area:mcp` or titled `MCP:` plan as `P5`; one WITH `bug` is a bug whatever its area. The 11 label-less MCP items (#1084, #1062, #1013, #962, #954, #937, #734, #732, #731, #730, #729) now plan as `P5` (dry-run, read-only, confirmed). Other label-less old-`P1`s are still listed for a hand check (none today).\r\n- Dry-run counts (main-broken empty, `--requested 530-548,617,661,1103,1104`): P1 5, P2 0, P3 17, P4 20, P5 25, P6 22, P7 20, P8 51; `P?` 5 (three lose a stray `P2`: #655, #658, #659); 19 untriaged. Issues filed since will differ.\r\n- An old-style `P1` filed while the migration runs must be re-rated by hand.\r\n- The end check fails (exit 1, lists them) until the 19 untriaged issues have a priority. Chosen: the runner triages those first (no new flag; simplest).\r\n",
